  "narrative": {
    "intro": "South National for Logistics has received $275M in federal contract obligations through FY2026 to date. South National for Logistics won 52 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $5.3M. South National for Logistics grew obligations up 136.6% year over year, reflecting a sharp increase compared with prior years. South National for Logistics recorded a steady increase in annual obligations from $0 in FY21 to $14.4M in FY22, $43.6M in FY23, $86.8M in FY24, and $116M in FY25 before reaching $275M in FY26. South National for Logistics figures are partial because FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than current-year obligations. South National for Logistics activity to date suggests the company is handling larger or more numerous awards this fiscal year compared with the prior year, and the average award size provides a sense of contract scale for procurement officers and prime contractors evaluating the vendor.",
